<title>GERMANY: Waigel says U.S. economy driving dollar rise.</title>
<headline>Waigel says U.S. economy driving dollar rise.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Finance Minister Theo Waigel said on Wednesday that he considered the recent strength of the dollar to be a reflection of the strong economy in the United States, not speculation about European economic and monetary union (EMU).</p>
<p>&quot;I don't believe the dollar's strength is a result of EMU speculation, Waigel said, referring to the idea that the mark is weakening because German participation in monetary union would wed it to weaker currencies.</p>
<p>&quot;U.S. growth is the main cause (for the dollar's strength),&quot; he said responding to questions by parliament's finance committee.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097 150</p>
